# Essence of Antiquity (1/10, Disguise {2}{W}): "When this creature is turned face up, creatures you control gain hexproof until end of turn. Untap them." (CR 702.168d,
# 701.40b, 603.2, 702.11b, 701.26b). Bot1 casts it face down with a Black Lotus and a Memnite, and attacks with the Memnite on turn 3 (it taps). In its second main phase
# Bot1 turns the Essence up for exactly {2}{W}: the trigger untaps the Memnite and the Essence and gives both hexproof. Bot2's Lightning Bolt is refused on the Memnite that
# turn, but Bot2's Memnite, not Bot1's, has no hexproof. On turn 4 (hexproof is over) the same Bolt on Bot1's Memnite is allowed and kills it.

